[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its reports hold more than one bug.
They were merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and the
subject only says "the date is wrong". It never says why.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued under #4471 fixes the parser only. The other rows below stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How each report was placed

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads dates month first, and every tenant on file writes the day
  first, so day and month come out flipped. Placed by `causeOf()` in `causes.ts`, by tenant and
  channel, not by `intakeTag`.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants. People type what the hint
  says and the form reads it day first. Only reports through the form of a booking-v3 tenant.
  Fixing the parser does not touch these.
- **`one-day shift`**: the date is not flipped, it moves by a day, and people in different places see
  different days for one booking. These are the reports in `desk-notes.json` (`oneDayMove`). The
  #4471 page counts them under `parser` and only footnotes them.

Each row has its own ticket with its count and example reports.

## For triage

Two reports with the same subject can have different causes, and two with different subjects can
share one. Before merging into a big ticket, check the tenant and channel with the
[explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe), and read the body: a one-day move is not a month/day flip.

